  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Degenerate orbitals of <math><msup><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>Cr</mtext><msub><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>2</mtext></mrow></msub><mtext>O</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mtext>6</mtext></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mtext>3+</mtext></mrow></msup></math>:&nbsp;</p><p>Orbitals having same energy call degenerate orbital, And here water acts as weak&nbsp;ligands which split&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>-</mo></math>orbital into two parts.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/dd45e518-c4e3-4574-9119-b7f13c75f68f-image13.png\" /><br />Hence, according to the options given, degenerate orbitals are <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></msub></math>.&nbsp;</p>",
